From f8975a9a02ef823b83e718782d18d055bb68e23c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Teemu Haila <teemu.haila@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:23:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] drm/amd/display: don't retrain the Apple 5K second tile
 on a post-training alignment blip

On the stitched iMac20,2 panel, about half of all DPMS wakes fail link 1's
post-training check: 5 ms after the idle pattern, DPCD 0x204 reads 0x80
(interlane alignment lost) although clock recovery, EQ and alignment all
completed during training. DC counts a link loss and retrains, up to four
times with 100/150/200 ms pauses, each an independent coin flip (about 0.5
each over 100 wakes), and enables the stream after the fourth loss anyway.
About 6 % of wakes lose all four; those are the wakes where the root tile
shows stretched over the panel for up to a second.

Polling the status for 100 ms instead of sampling once showed the sink
never realigns while the idle pattern runs (27 of 27 losses over 20 wakes),
but every one of those wakes was healthy at the next link-health pass,
~400 ms later, with no retrain: the sink realigns once video flows.

For the Apple tiled slave only, log the blip and let the stream start, as
DC already does for eDP. A real loss is still caught by the stitch's
link-health check, which retrains the link and escalates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c       | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c
index a8678b9ea..12b0654a5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_training.c
@@ -1549,6 +1549,24 @@ static enum link_training_result dp_transition_to_video_idle(
 			msleep(5);
 			if (!link->skip_fallback_on_link_loss)
 				status = dp_check_link_loss_status(link, lt_settings);
+			/*
+			 * Apple 5K second tile: on about half of all wakes its TCON
+			 * reports interlane alignment lost (0x204=80) right after
+			 * training, although CR, EQ and alignment all completed. It
+			 * stays that way while the idle pattern runs (polled for
+			 * 100 ms: never back), and realigns by itself once video
+			 * flows: the link-health pass ~400 ms later finds it aligned
+			 * with no retrain. Treating it as a loss retrains up to four
+			 * times while the root tile shows stretched over the panel,
+			 * and DC enables the stream after the fourth anyway. So let
+			 * the stream start, as for eDP, and leave a real loss to the
+			 * stitch's link-health check, which retrains and escalates.
+			 */
+			if (status == LINK_TRAINING_LINK_LOSS && dc_link_is_apple_tiled_slave(link)) {
+				DC_LOG_INFO("APPLE5K: link[%u] alignment not reported 5 ms after training; leaving it to link-health\n",
+					    link->link_index);
+				status = LINK_TRAINING_SUCCESS;
+			}
 		}
 		return status;
 	}
